  "final_answer_preview": "In this scenario, the group can be charged with criminal conspiracy under Section 61(1)(b) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, which defines a criminal conspiracy as an agreement to commit an offence, provided that some act is done in pursuance of that agreement. Since the group was caught before committing the offence, they may also be subject to punishment for an attempt under Section 61(2)(b), which addresses the punishment for attempting to commit offences. Additionally, if the conspiracy involved a terrorist act, Section 113(3) would apply, imposing a more severe penalty.",
